T+  0.0  The battery in A5 is overheating. The site operator has raised the alarm.
T+  6.7  A5 is venting flammable gas. Its battery is in thermal runaway.
T+  9.0  Pumper 1 on scene.
--- decision 1 at T+9.0: Pumper 1 is the first crew on scene. Time for a first plan.
   [32s, tools: get_situation,get_sensor_check,get_forecast,read_lessons,test_plan,test_plan,test_plan] Cool A6 now and A4 when Pumper 2 arrives
     - Pumper 1 cools A6: Cool the warmer neighbour before fire heats it further.
     - Pumper 2 cools A4: Protect the other close neighbour immediately on arrival.
     why: Keep crews north and at least 17 m from venting A5. Two streams prevent predicted spread as effectively as three, while current wind carries smoke away from Glenvale homes and Glenvale Primary.
     sensor: The wind reading has no independent smoke check yet.
     sensor: Fixed gas readings are noisy and remain unverified by HAZMAT 1.
     effect: Enclosures involved after 40 minutes: 3.1 -> 1.0
T+  9.3  A5 is on fire.
